Sven,

it is a known bug in some Java packages. First, make sure you are  
using Java 1.6 or higher. If you are not, upgrade first as versions  
1.5 and earlier are broken on x86_64 platforms. Secondly if you have  
SuSE's JDK 1.6 package and the error still persists, install Sun's  
official JDK package instead. We found that some distributions have  
broken Java setup and installing Sun's version helps.

Cheers,
Simon

