.. and you are using IDEs that are as old as Knuth's TeX I  
suppose ;)? Breaking text at xx columns in sources is IMHO really  
stupid, because it doesn't allow you to view the code at any other  
width, smaller or bigger (just look at e-mails for example - if one  
person uses such a dumb e-mail client, it makes all the follow-ups  
virtually unreadable, because the lines are double-broken). Any  
reasonable editor allows soft-wrap (possibly an intelligent one)  
which is far more pleasant to read (to me). Moreover, source code is  
not flow text ;).

But back to the actual issue - the files were edited by different  
people with different editors. I prefer tabs and soft-wrap, because  
that leaves everything up to your editor and personally I use mostly  
Xcode which works just fine for this and shows everything nicely  
aligned, but others don't. Usually I avoid committing whitespace- 
changes, because it muds vc history unnecessarily.


