> describing a pointer to a structure in R memory and on the other  
> hand it describes a pure java structure which will eventually be  
> assigned by the Rengine into the R memory space.
>
>         Is this dual role necessary or could REXP be split into REXP
>         which would point to an object in R memory and JRIEXP (or some
>         other) which would be a pure Java construct?
>

The dual role is again historical. It is an amalgam of the original  
JRI REXP code where it was purely a direct reference and Rserve's  
REXP which is driven by the copied representation. This was done at a  
point where I was designing a new prototype that would abstract out  
the back-end, so the mixture was put in JRI for compatibility, such  
that other projects can still use it. However, there were technical  
issues with the prototype because it would break existing rJava  
package, so it is currently on hold as I'm adding other features to  
rJava right now.

Cheers,
Simon

