The result of 1 means that the JVM is already running, so .jinit just  
attached to it. This is no error, it just means that you cannot set  
the JVM parameters (such as -X...), because it's up already, possibly  
started by another package that has been loaded.


>
> Prob2 - jcall
> - adding classes through classpath in jinit  I can only call class  
> methods which have no parameters. However I can 'see' them  
> with .jmethods. Could you show me examples, let say, to pass  
> integers or doubles to class methods ?
> Do we have to cast for these types ?   I used i.e.  :
>
> s1<-47.33
> x<-2
> y<-4
>  .jcall(ts, "V", "setSymbP", x, y, s1)         //   [3] "public  
> void ibr.Tsymboles.setSymbP(int,int,double)"
>

Look at

 > typeof(x)
[1] "double"

A common mistake is to assume that 1 is an integer (in R ;)).   
Normally all numbers are by default doubles, so you have to convert  
them to integers if you really mean that. In your case you probably  
want to use

.jcall(ts, "V",  "setSymbP", as.integer(x), as.integer(y), s1)

When using this in a function, it is a good idea to cast s1 with  
as.double(s1) as well.

Cheers,
Simon

